# Workflow scripts are read from disk and passed through a permission dialog that rejects control
# characters, so a CRLF checkout makes them unrunnable. Keep them LF on every platform.
*.js text eol=lf
# .mjs is the same rule and was missed until 2026-08-21, when the eval harness could not be
# launched: evals/harness/*.mjs had been pure CRLF since it was written, and the permission
# dialog rejected it as containing control characters. The comment above named that exact
# failure while its own pattern did not cover the file it was written to protect.
*.mjs text eol=lf
# atlas.html is written by tools/gen-atlas.py with newline="
", so pinning it keeps a fresh
# checkout byte-identical to what the generator produces. Added 2026-08-22 alongside *.mjs.
*.html text eol=lf

# The gate and its tools are executed by CI on Linux and locally on Windows; LF everywhere avoids
# a class of shebang and heredoc breakage that only shows up on one of the two.
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Prose and data files were left unpinned until 2026-08-07, so on Windows every `git add` printed a
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning for each one: dozens per bundle PR, enough that a real warning
# would have been lost in them. The gate and the CI steps read these files on Linux and locally on
# Windows, and the repo-wide dash sweep reads them byte by byte, so one ending everywhere is also one
# fewer difference between what CI sees and what an author sees.
*.md text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# The site (S0) brings four file shapes this list never had to cover, and `git add` warned on every
# one of them. `.nvmrc` is the dangerous member: CI reads it through `node-version-file`, so a CRLF
# checkout hands setup-node a version string with a trailing carriage return. This is the *.mjs
# lesson repeated - that pattern was missed until 2026-08-21, when the eval harness could not start
# because its files had been pure CRLF since the day they were written, under a comment describing
# the exact failure its own pattern did not cover. A new toolchain brings new extensions; pin them
# when it lands, not after something will not start.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
# *.mdx was missed on the first pass of this very block, on 2026-09-18, and caught two days later
# when `git add` warned on the site's two narrative pages. Twice now this list has been extended
# while leaving out a shape sitting in the same commit. If you add a type here, run `git add` over
# the whole tree and read every warning before believing the list is complete.
*.mdx text eol=lf
.nvmrc text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
